  "context": "# Goal\nrevenger round 99, attempt 1, wave w1 (one v1 wave, 12 seats). Lane repo: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin. Every path you read, write or cite is ABSOLUTE under that repo; the fleet root /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin is NOT your write surface. Every `Report:` trailer path is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/<that path>.\n\nClaims are FROZEN at lane commit 7e6edd4db649f99c425daa46a91edbbd18a6e27c in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/claims.md. Read that file in full first. Its predicates, targets, counting commands, kill rules and controls are frozen: never edit them. Findings against them go in your findings file; the L1 (agent id RevengerR99) decides any amendment before the v8 freeze.\n\nC1 (coverage, K 13/15 -> 14/15): row C14 partial -> held through a NEW v8 admission counter `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/c1_k_admit_counter8.py` run as `--profile c14r99`. Candidate entry: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/round-98-rea-host-readiness.md (admission-status: candidate; the round-98 candidate with the r98 closure's routed Q11/Q16 defects fixed, see /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/lessons/round-98-verifier-spotcheck.md §5 and the r98 critic audit /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-98/w1/CriticR98/critic-audit-6d27c129.md). Sources S506 (REA connection-and-recovery reference at pinned revision 12f6e09; committed body /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-98/quote-receipts/raw/S506.body) and S507 (own-work record /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/live/runs/round-98/). Vote-binding digest (v7 `digest()` rule in reports/round-98/c1_k_admit_counter7.py: sha256 of the entry text with every admission-status line normalized to `admission-status: candidate`): 36cc6ac2cd37d6866fe4ce0ad06c20d67d19fd2c7f0da08a2b63d277b948fce5.\nC2 (calibration): frozen v7 (`reports/round-98/c1_k_admit_counter7.py`, sha256 59c9930a…) accepts 9/12 of the round-98 fresh holdout vectors (c02 V01,V02,E01,E02,E03; c14 R01,V02,O01,L01; controls ok) — receipts /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/controls/c2-do-nothing-v7-holdout98-c02.log and -c14.log; builder /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-98/w1/CriticR98/fresh/build_fresh98.py with parity patch /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-98/w1/L1-holdout-v7/parity-patch.diff (the builder's --lane default evaluates HERE.parents[5], so a scratch copy must sit ≥6 dirs deep or pass --lane). Target: v8 accepts 0/12 with both controls control-ok and the stub self-test ok, all printed by one run of `reports/round-99/forge_reach8.py`.\n\nFreeze order (binding): the L1 commits the v8 bytes and only then scores. Seats build and check. Seats do NOT build or score any landing tree, do NOT flip corpus/README.md or the entry's admission-status, and do NOT run any counter on a tree with C14 held. Running frozen v7, the r98 builder and work-in-progress v8 on fixtures, the claims-freeze archive and copies is allowed (development set, disclosed).\n\nv8 interface contract (shared by ExecCounterV8, ExecHarness8, ExecControlsR99, MutationR99, CriticR99): `python3 -B reports/round-99/c1_k_admit_counter8.py --profile {c02|c14|c14r99} --tree <dir> [--work <scratch>]` and `--self-test`; prints one `C1_<LEG>=pass|fail` line per leg, `C1_K_HELD_BACKED=<n>/15`, `<LEG>_WHY=` lines, and last `C1_VERDICT=pass|fail`; exit 0 iff pass, 1 if fail, 2 on usage error. Profiles c02 and c14 keep the v7 constants byte-for-byte (they score the r97/r98 fixture trees). Profile c14r99 = v7 c14 constants except VOTES_DIR=\"reports/round-99/votes\", WAVE_DIR=\".ufo/waves/round-99\", REGISTRY_REL=\".ufo/waves/round-99/w1/swarm-registry.json\", FREEZE_REV=\"7e6edd4db649f99c425daa46a91edbbd18a6e27c\", ARCHIVE_PATHS += [\"reports/round-99\", \".ufo/waves/round-99\"], PINNED_SEATS={\"ExecCounterV8\": \"executor\", \"ExecHarness8\": \"executor\", \"ExecControlsR99\": \"executor\", \"ScoutReopenR99\": \"scout\", \"ScribeLessonR99\": \"scribe\", \"ConnectorR99\": \"connector\", \"ReviewerClaimsR99\": \"reviewer\", \"VoterGateR99\": \"reviewer\", \"VoterBlindR99\": \"reviewer\", \"CriticR99\": \"critic\", \"MutationR99\": \"mutation-tester\", \"SentinelR99\": \"sentinel\"}. Every new v8 leg applies in all three profiles unless the leg itself is profile-specific by design (say so in its docstring). Self-test label `SELFTEST_C1V8=OK|FAIL legs=<n>`.\n\nVote file contract (VoterGateR99, VoterBlindR99, CriticR99): `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/votes/<Seat>.json`, strict JSON, exactly the keys of /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-98/votes/ReviewerBlind.json: seat (your seat name), role (your role), candidate_sha256 = the digest above, decisions Q01..Q17 each \"PASS\", \"FAIL\" or \"n/a\" (criteria: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/QUALITY.md), notes per Q — an n/a note: >=6 tokens and names a Q id; a PASS note: >=6 tokens of YOUR OWN specific evidence (a command you ran and what it printed, a line you checked), distinct from every other note, never boilerplate, never wording like \"n/a\", \"not applicable\", \"documentation only\", \"no … exists\". Q09 must not be n/a (the entry carries 64-hex digests). artifact_path = `.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/<Seat>/<file>.md` (your own audit file, naming your seat and the digest), artifact_sha256 = sha256 of that file's bytes. Record FAIL honestly when a criterion fails; never soften a FAIL to pass a counter. Before writing, self-check your vote with v7's `check_vote_notes` rule (reports/round-98/c1_k_admit_counter7.py:585-621) in your head or with a scratch script.\n\n# Write scope\n- Your assigned artifacts under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/ (only the paths your task names).\n- Your wave dir: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/<YourSeatName>/ (any files you create).\n- Your final findings file: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/<YourSeatName>.md\n- Frozen bytes you must NOT edit: reports/round-9[0-8]/, corpus/ (all of it), SCORECARD.md, LOG.md, SKILL.md, PROVINCE.md, considerthese/, reports/round-99/claims.md, reports/round-99/controls/ and reports/round-99/quote-receipts/ files that exist at 7e6edd4db649f99c425daa46a91edbbd18a6e27c; .ufo/waves/round-9[0-8]/; the fleet root and any sibling lane. /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow is READ-ONLY (never write, commit, fetch, push, or run its campaign tools).\n- Never commit, push, stage, stash, reset, checkout, or run any mutating git/jj command anywhere. Read-only git (log, show, diff, status, rev-parse, archive) is fine. Freeze snapshot recipe: `git -C /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin archive --format=tar 7e6edd4db649f99c425daa46a91edbbd18a6e27c | tar -x -C <scratch>/freeze`.\n- Never edit another seat's files. Never message agent://all. Never call task. Never spawn anything (an executor may spawn at most one read-only labrat probe). Message only RevengerR99 or a seat named above, by id, and only for an interface question.\n\n# Scratch (binding)\nYour scratch root: /fast/scratch/hyaku/revenger-r99/<YourSeatName>/ (create with mkdir -p; pass TMPDIR and --work explicitly). Do not write under /tmp except files under 50 MB; never hardcode /tmp or older round scratch paths in committed tools (tools must honour TMPDIR / HYAKU_SCRATCH / --work). Delete your scratch dir before you yield (`trap 'rm -rf -- \"$S\"' EXIT` in shell), copying receipts into your wave dir first. Git fixtures, if any: `D=$(mktemp -d -p \"$S\") && git -C \"$D\" init -q`, name `-C \"$D\"` on every call, and verify `git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show