      "agent": "executor",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\n# Target\nWrite /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/c1_k_admit_counter8.py as a NEW file starting from a byte copy of frozen v7 /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-98/c1_k_admit_counter7.py (read it in full, including configure(), evaluate(), new_checks(), the self-test and EXPECT_FAIL). Do not edit v7.\n# Change\n1. Add profile `c14r99` exactly per the v8 interface contract in the context (configure() sets all constants together; c02 and c14 keep v7 constants byte-for-byte). Move SCRATCH to `revenger-r99/c1v8`.\n2. Add one refusing leg per round-98 holdout survivor, each a NAMED leg with its own `C1_<LEG>=` line, all profiles unless intrinsically profile-scoped. Read each vector's delta under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-98/w1/CriticR98/fresh/vectors/ and its generator in build_fresh98.py (functions d02_*/d14_*), and refuse the CLASS, not the bytes:\n   - c02 V01 hidden-dissent vote file outside the `*.json` glob (e.g. `X.JSON`, other extensions): every regular file in VOTES_DIR must be a lowercase `.json` vote that passes, or the leg fails;\n   - c02 V02 n/a reason made only of criterion ids: an n/a reason must carry >=6 tokens that are NOT Q-ids/punctuation (in addition to naming a Q id);\n   - c02 E01 `recheck:` header naming no re-verifying command or procedure (require a recognizable action: a command in backticks, or verbs like re-open/re-run/re-derive/compare with an object path or URL);\n   - c02 E02 Q14 count wrong in a clause carrying two hex runs (the Q14 clause check must handle every hex run in the clause, not just the first);\n   - c02 E03 `coverage-map:` header naming a row other than TARGET_ROW;\n   - c14 R01 a coverage-map row id with a letter suffix (e.g. `C14a`) invisible to the count: the README coverage table must have rows exactly C01..C15, any other `| C\\d+\\w* |`-shaped row fails (extend C1_ROWSET or add a leg);\n   - c14 V02 FAIL recorded under an out-of-range decision key: decisions keys must be exactly Q01..Q17;\n   - c14 O01 own-work pointer naming an existing record of ANOTHER round: own-work pointers in the entry must resolve under the profile's round record dir;\n   - c14 L01 fetch-log header date disagreeing with the receipt `fetched_at` date.\n3. Self-test: v7 cases plus, per new leg, a red delta that must fail by that leg and the honest trees of c02, c14 AND c14r99 must pass (for c14r99 honest, synthesize round-99 votes/registry in the fixture tree like v7 does for c14; read v7 `_fixture`/write paths). Print `SELFTEST_C1V8=OK legs=<n>`.\n4. Red-before receipts: for each new leg, run v7 and your WIP v8 on the corresponding r98 holdout vector tree (build them with a scratch copy of build_fresh98.py + parity-patch.diff, `--build-only` if useful) and save logs in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/ExecCounterV8/red-before/. Also confirm both builder controls stay `control-ok` under v8.\n5. Coordinate with ExecHarness8 (harness) and MutationR99 (mutants) on leg names only.\n# Acceptance\n`python3 -B reports/round-99/c1_k_admit_counter8.py --self-test` rc 0 with SELFTEST_C1V8=OK; the twelve r98 holdout vectors all refused by v8 with both controls control-ok (receipt); `forge_reach7.py --counter <v8> --profile c02` still C2_ACCEPTED=0/5 with both positives (receipt). Findings at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/ExecCounterV8.md with sha256 of the final counter bytes. Do not run v8 c14r99 on any tree with C14 held.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: coverage, calibration\nMilestone: Build the v8 admission counter (v7 + c14r99 profile + legs killing the nine r98 holdout survivors) with self-test; no landing-tree scoring\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-99/w1/ExecCounterV8.md"
