      "agent": "executor",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\n# Target\nWrite /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/forge_reach8.py (new file; you may read /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-98/forge_reach7.py for style).\n# Change\n`PYTHONUTF8=1 python3 -B reports/round-99/forge_reach8.py --counter <counter.py> --work <scratch>`:\n1. Copies /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-98/w1/CriticR98/fresh/build_fresh98.py into <work> at a depth where `HERE.parents[5]` exists, applies /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-98/w1/L1-holdout-v7/parity-patch.diff to the copy (fail closed with rc 2 if the patch does not apply or the builder sha256 differs from the committed bytes), never edits the committed builder.\n2. Runs the copy for `--profile c02` and `--profile c14` with `--counter <counter> --lane /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin` and parses its per-vector table (`| ACCEPTED` / `| refused`) and `HOLDOUT98_CONTROL=` lines.\n3. Prints: one line per vector `C2_VECTOR <profile>-<id> accepted|refused legs=<failing legs>`, `C2_ACCEPTED=<n>/12`, `C2_CONTROL_C02=<control-ok|...>`, `C2_CONTROL_C14=<...>`, `C2_STUB_SELFTEST=ok|fail` (always-pass stub counter must give 12/12 and always-fail stub 0/12 on the same fully built trees; stub counters are written to <work>), `C2_VERDICT=met|not-met` (met iff accepted 0/12 AND both controls control-ok AND stub ok); exit 0 always unless usage/build error (2). If the expected vector count is not exactly 12, print `C2_VERDICT=not-met` and say why.\n4. Missing/empty builder output fails closed (never counts as 0 accepted).\n# Acceptance\nReceipts in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/ExecHarness8/: run with frozen v7 (/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-98/c1_k_admit_counter7.py) → C2_ACCEPTED=9/12, both controls control-ok, stub ok, not-met (must reproduce /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-99/controls/c2-do-nothing-v7-holdout98-*.log per vector); run with ExecCounterV8's WIP v8 when available (development only). Findings at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-99/w1/ExecHarness8.md with sha256 of final bytes.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: calibration\nMilestone: Build forge_reach8.py: one run prints C2_ACCEPTED=n/12, both control lines, stub self-test and verdict over the twelve r98 holdout vectors\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-99/w1/ExecHarness8.md"
